    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_fiber_two_cycle_c2_gap_only_parity_counterexample",
    "title": "Budget-three fiber-two c=2 gaps alone do not force parity",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "Over F_53 at H=8, the split squarefree quartic E(z)=1+z+11z^2+34z^3+43z^4 has a_14=a_15=0, a_16=2, and its normalized two-window product LT/2 is the square of 1+22z+49z^2+3z^3+16z^4 modulo z^8. Its four roots are not two-antipodal. Their orders are 52,13,13,52 and their square classes are mixed, so the example refutes gap-only parity forcing but not the official torsion-and-square implication.",
